# Frontend UX

Design mobile-first for a homeowner on an iPhone. The public page has one job: call, or finish the short form. Use Tailwind 4 utilities. Add tokens in `@theme` inside `app/globals.css`. Do not add a legacy `tailwind.config.js`.

## Layout

- Base styles are the phone. Add `sm:` and `md:` only when the layout needs more room.
- Inputs use at least `text-base` (16px) so iOS does not zoom on focus.
- Tap targets are at least 44px. The phone number is a `tel:` link in a bar fixed to the bottom, with `pb` and `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` so it does not cover the form.
- One primary action per screen. Keep listings, blog, and chat widgets off the seller hero.

## Access

- Label every input. Do not rely on placeholder text alone.
- Keep a visible focus ring. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` by skipping nonessential transitions.
- Motion is limited to color, opacity, and short transforms on hover or press.

```tsx
<a href="tel:+16025550100" className="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center px-4">
  Call Vamos
</a>
```
